<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Argos and Nauplia</h1><p class="st-meta">1212 CE – 1388 CE · capital Nauplia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Frankish lordship of the Argolid, held by the lords of Athens and their heirs, which ended when its last lady sold it to Venice in 1388.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-sgouros">Leo Sgouros</a>, his last strongholds, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argos">Argos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a>, fell to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a> in 1212. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea</a> granted them to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otho-de-la-roche">Otho de la Roche</a>, lord of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-athens">Duchy of Athens</a>, who held them as a fief of the prince.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>For a century the lordship was held by the dukes of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a>, giving them a foothold in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> and a port at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a>. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-company">Catalans</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> in 1311, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> and Nauplia stayed loyal to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-brienne">Brienne</a> heirs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-v-of-brienne">Walter of Brienne</a> and later passed to the Enghien family. Greek and Albanian farmers worked the fertile Argive plain.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Pressed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/despotate-of-the-morea">Despotate of the Morea</a> and the Turks, the heiress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marie-of-enghien">Marie of Enghien</a> sold the lordship to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1388. The Despot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-i-palaiologos">Theodore I</a> seized <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/argos">Argos</a> first, but Venice took control, creating <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/venetian-nauplia">Venetian Nauplia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1212 CE – 1388 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.82%;width:3.50%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1212 CE – 1388 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nauplia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Otho de la Roche, Marie of Enghien</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity (rulers), Eastern Orthodox Christianity (population)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French, Medieval Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Argos and Nauplia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1300&amp;focus=lordship-of-argos-and-nauplia" aria-label="Lordship of Argos and Nauplia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5250 826 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Argos and Nauplia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5570 1082L5530 1071M5570 1082L5580 1057M5570 1082L5293 831M5570 1082L5570 1082"/><path class="ma